==Battleground==
*1 [[Berserkory]] spawns after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*2 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn as bosses after 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**2 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn as bosses, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
**1 [[Razorback]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**2 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn as bosses, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
**1 [[Bun Bun Symbiote]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**2 [[Squire Rel]]s spawn as bosses, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
**1 [[Angelic Sleipnir]] spawns.
**1 [[Boraphim]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Looking at the roster of enemies, you'll need to build a lineup that includes units that can counter and defeat each enemy. The presence of Razorback requires the usage of [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bomber Cat]], and the Boraphim is best countered by a unit such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]]. As for the Berserkory and Bun Bun Symbiote, [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] is good enough to counter both, to stop Berserkory's Waves and counter Bun Bun Symbiote's Floating trait. Talented [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] serves as a counter to all enemies in this stage, especially the Boraphim. One thing to note while fighting Bun Bun Symbiote is that you should be careful to not push him behind his base thanks to his many knockbacks, as fighting him along with Boraphim and Sleipnir can be a death sentence. If one has [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], he can easily melt down the Berserkory and eventually chip down the Sleipnir. All in all, consider this stage as a unit check for each of your different units.

